Date: Thu, 30 Dec 93 03:16:13 EST
From: Harvey Newstrom <hnewstrom@hnewstrom.ess.harris.com>
Subject: PPLs: It's not a Perfect System (yet)

This whole implementation of List Rules by ExI fiat and PPL Law 
independently administered still has some bugs in it.  This is not a list 
of complaints, nor do I wish any action to be taken based on my comments 
below.  But, I think people around here need to realize that we are still 
experimenting.  The implementation of Law on this list is not clear-cut or 
obvious!  The system does not handle legal problems in the manner predicted 
by PPL theories.  In the last 48-hours the following anomalies have 
personally occurred to me:

1. The List Administrator publically posts that serious List Rules have 
been broken, but no action will be taken.

2. A judgement is made on the grounds that a person brought charges against 
himself, which he denies doing.  (These were later dropped.)

3. A harsher-than-normal punishment is given with a rider that it will 
probably never be enforced.

4. Tim May says he ignored a report of a crime from PPL-1 to his PPL and 
Harry never continued the issue.  This may be the first intra-PPL 
arbitration, and it fell through the cracks!

5. An entire legal battle (hnewstrom vs. /hawk) was waged without involving 
the PPL system.  I was blocked from "criminal" activity (trying to become 
an outlaw), appealed, had the appeal denied all without using PPLs, the 
List Arbitor, or the List Judge.  (Harry claims no "judgement" occurred, 
just a "statement of fact!")  This may be the first "attempted crime" since 
multiple PPLs have existed, and the resolution seems to have completely 
side-stepped all components of the PPL system.

6. I filed an appeal of Harry's decision via e-mail to the List Arbitor and 
had Harry deny the appeal without the List Arbitor even acknowledging the 
e-mail.

7. Harry enforced "List Rules" that he says have been in place from the 
beginning which it turns out were never actually written down anywhere.  
(They will be added to the next publication of the List Rules.)

8. Multiple people have announced and/or referenced the creation of PPLs 
that are not actually sanctioned by ExI.  (I don't know about PPL-Anarchy, 
but when I checked 48 hours ago there were still only PPL-1 and PPL-May.)

9. There seems to be confusion over whether PPLs must obey List Laws.  ExI 
will enforce their rules "by fiat" while we are told other PPLs should not 
have the same rules as PPL-1 or they would be redundant.

10. My PPL founder and coordinator posts publically that I am no longer in 
his PPL.  He further states that my PPL has been approved.  I was never 
informed of these events, and do not believe they have yet happened.

11. Tim publically admits that his joking remarks about a PPL was 
sanctioned by ExI as an official PPL.  He says he never went through any of 
the so-called requirements for forming a PPL.  Other people have seriously 
tried creating PPLs without (as yet) success.

(P.S.  My PPL attempt is still planned and underway.  It will probably take 
me a few weeks before I am ready to file the required documentation.)
__
