From: cards@top.cis.syr.edu
Subject: PPLs: It's not a Perfect System (yet)

I have followed this whole PPL thing lately and would like
to point out one major cause of the confusion: imprecise
communication.  Writers need to be more careful to post
exactly what they mean, and to state things clearly,
using the appropriate grammatical clues (subjunctive
vs indicative, conditional, etc.)  Readers need to read
posts carefully, try to ascertain what the writer intended
(vs what the reader wishes the writer had intended) and
respond rationally (rather than shoot from the hip with
rebuttals which seem based upon the premise that all
posts by others are attacks).

IOW:
Say what you mean, mean what you say, and assume that
others mean exactly what they say (neither more nor less).
English is an incredibly powerful language.  Use it.
