Subject: PHIL: Balanced Reality

This post uses the aspects of reality I posted in "PHIL: Consensual Reality", it
is a bonus follow-up brought on by popular demand.  A brief recap of that post
would be: Objective Reality, Subjective Reality, and Consensual Reality.  All
exist simultaneously and inseparably (Monist indeed!).

These three aspects of reality are equally balanced, consider them as attractors
in aspectual reality space.  Extropy is maximum when a stable periodic orbit
around the three attractors is achieved, analogous to a stable three partner
firm or three equal owners of a business or three equal participants in an
alliance.  Without energy input into this balanced state, or with small
perturbations, it is easily knocked down to a periodic orbit around two
attractors.  As often happens in human arrangements, two entities decide that
the third entity is "less equal" (aka "the squeeze").  Lesser amounts of energy
must be input into the two attractor orbit but the same result occurs if
perturbed or if energy input drops off; a reversion to the most entropic level
of a periodic orbit around one attractor.  In human arrangements, one entity
achieves a status of "more equal" than the others (aka the buyout or power
play).

The most extropic state is keeping an equal balance between "They" (objective
reality) - "We" (consensual reality) - "I" (subjective reality).  This is very
difficult to do, it requires much energy input (exertion of willpower towards
this specific purpose).  The following is a list of some the shortcomings of two
attractor and one attractor orbits in aspectual reality space:

One attractor orbits
 "I" - too much subjectivity, faith, mysticism, paranoia, egomania, absolutism
(religious type), loss of meaning.
 "We" - a downgrading of both fact and value, politicians, pragmatists,
expediency and purposelessness.
 "They" - too much objectivity, loss of meaning, values, and purpose; French
post-structuralist, nihilism, absolute relativism.

Two attractor orbits
 "I"|"We" - loss of regard for fact, technological stagnation, organized
religion.
 "We"|"They" - loss of regard for individual purpose and self-determination,
Hegelian dialectical materialism tradition, statist.
 "They"|"I" - loss of meaning, difficulty achieving increasing civilization
levels, Objectivists.

Each of these could be expanded on; of course there are overlaps, these are
pseudo-archetypes, not absolutes.  This topic could be reposted as "Unbalanced
Reality" for those who prefer a two or one attractor orbit.

